---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Walk Studios | Memphis Web Design Studio"
  description="Walk Studios is a one-person studio run by Brian Peterson — CS degree, PMP certified, and former construction math instructor. Senior technical depth without agency overhead."
  canonical="/about"
>
  <div class="pt-32 pb-16 min-h-screen">
    <!-- Top logo watermark + tagline -->
    <div class="relative">
      <img
        class="w-screen left-1/2 transform -translate-x-1/2 opacity-10"
        alt="crosswalk logo watermark"
        src="/Images/Walk_Logo_2.svg"
        width="1200"
        height="400"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 flex flex-row items-center mt-28 md:mt-0">
        <div class="md:mt-12 grid grid-cols-1">
          <p
            class="mt-12 sm:pt-12 lg:mt-0 lg:pt-0 text-2xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl mx-5 md:mx-11"
          >
            Good design is only half the job. The other half is making sure the
            right people find it, trust it, and act on it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4">
      <!-- Bio section -->
      <div class="mt-52 lg:mt-40">
        <img
          class="w-full"
          alt="Brian Peterson, founder and developer at Walk Studios"
          src="/Images/Brian.jpg"
          width="800"
          height="600"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-4xl mt-4">BRIAN PETERSON</h2>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-500 mt-1">Founder | Developer</p>
        <div class="mt-4 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed space-y-3">
          <p>
            Brian holds a B.S. in Computer Science from the University of
            Memphis and a PMP certification — the technical depth to build
            complex systems and the discipline to deliver them on schedule.
          </p>
          <p>
            In 2026 he built TradePathHub from scratch — a 2,800+ URL
            programmatic platform on Next.js with ISR, Sanity CMS, a live
            affiliate system, and real organic search traffic. Solo. That build
            set the bar every client project gets measured against.
          </p>
          <p>
            Walk Studios exists because most small businesses deserve better
            than a template site that nobody finds. Every project is scoped
            clearly, built correctly, and delivered with copy and structure that
            actually converts.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Services section -->
      <div class="mt-12 mb-16">
        <div class="space-y-12">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold">STRATEGY</h3>
            <div class="bg-black h-1 w-full mt-2 mb-3"></div>
            <ul class="text-2xl space-y-1">
              <li>Branding</li>
              <li>SEO</li>
              <li>Content Strategy</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold">DESIGN</h3>
            <div class="bg-black h-1 w-full mt-2 mb-3"></div>
            <ul class="text-2xl space-y-1">
              <li>Web</li>
              <li>Graphic</li>
              <li>UX/UI</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold">DEVELOPMENT</h3>
            <div class="bg-black h-1 w-full mt-2 mb-3"></div>
            <ul class="text-2xl space-y-1">
              <li>Web</li>
              <li>E-commerce Integration</li>
              <li>CMS Integration</li>
              <li>Performance & SEO</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="mt-24 flex flex-col items-center text-center px-4">
      <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold">
        Ready to build something that works?
      </p>
      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="mt-6 inline-block bg-walk-red text-white px-6 py-3"
      >
        Let's Talk →
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
